  "worked_solution": "The diameter can be calculated using the distance formula: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\sqrt{{({x}_{1}-{x}_{2})}^{2}+{({y}_{1}-{y}_{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-6-6)^{2}+(-4-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-12)^{2}+(-5)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{144+25} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{169} \\\\  & =13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe radius is half the diameter:\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{d}{2}=\\frac{13}{2}\n$$",
